      "title": "Marginal Tax Rates",
      "description": "Hong Kong's maximum tax (the \"standard rate\") has normally been 15 percent, effectively capping the marginal rate at high income levels (in exchange for no personal exemptions). The highest U.S. tax rate of 39.6 percent after 1993 was reduced to 38.6 percent in 2002 and to 35 percent in 2003.",
